([2, 0, 0]):(-1)

// What is true of the selection, for the ribbon to show (docs/QUILL.md 4.3): for a flag (ed_s_flag plus a quill_flag_* bit) 0 off, 1 on, 2 mixed; for a character field (a quill_character_* offset) its effective value or -2 when the selection mixes values; for a paragraph field (ed_s_para plus a quill_paragraph_* offset) likewise. With nothing selected it describes the text the next typed character takes.
editor_selection_state(Doc d, Ctl ctl, int field) {
  int[] acc = (import editor_sample_cells);
  lset(acc, 0, field);
  lset(acc, 1, 0);
} chain (Doc d, Ctl ctl, int field) {
  lset(acc, 2, 0);
  editor_selection_walk(d, ctl, acc);
  int res = editor_selection_answer(acc);
} return int res;
